arguments.prompt:
You are working in /tmp/sv-52cefc34d75346d5ba30c44e6fd71bf4/ShipmentTracker which contains a Blazor Web App scaffolded with `dotnet new blazor -int Auto -ai -au Individual`. It has two projects:
- `ShipmentTracker/` (server project)
- `ShipmentTracker.Client/` (client/WebAssembly project)

This is an Interactive Auto Global app — all interactive components go in the `.Client` project. Components cannot access DbContext directly; they must use HTTP APIs via service interfaces.

## Task

Implement a logistics shipment tracking app with these features:

### 1. Create AGENTS.md in the server project root (`ShipmentTracker/AGENTS.md`) with this content (replace {AppName} with ShipmentTracker):

```
# ShipmentTracker

| Setting | Value |
|---------|-------|
| **Interactivity Mode** | Auto |
| **Interactivity Scope** | Global |

## Rendering configuration
This project uses global Interactive Auto with prerendering.
Created with `dotnet new blazor -int Auto -ai -au Individual`.

On a user's first visit, components render via Interactive Server (SignalR). On subsequent visits the cached WebAssembly runtime takes over and interactions run entirely in the browser.

## Project structure
- **ShipmentTracker** (server): Hosts the Blazor app, serves static files, API endpoints.
- **ShipmentTracker.Client** (WebAssembly): All interactive UI components. Run on server first, then browser.

## Adding new components
- Interactive components MUST go in the `.Client` project, not the server project.
- New pages go in `ShipmentTracker.Client/Pages/`.
- All pages are already interactive (global mode). No need to add `@rendermode` to individual components.
- Server-only static components (e.g., error pages) belong in the server `Components/` folder.

## Data access
Interactive components cannot access the database directly. Use this pattern:
1. Define an interface in the `.Client` project (e.g., `IDataService`).
2. In the `.Client` project, implement it using `HttpClient` to call server APIs.
3. In the server project, implement it using direct data access (EF Core DbContext, etc.).
4. Register the client implementation in the client `Program.cs` and the server implementation in the server `Program.cs`.
5. Expose server data through minimal API endpoints (e.g., `app.MapGet(...)`) that the client implementation calls.
6. If the page requires authorization, apply the same auth policy to both the Blazor page (`@attribute [Authorize]`) and the minimal API endpoint (`.RequireAuthorization()`).

## Authentication
ASP.NET Core Identity is configured with individual accounts. Identity pages under `Components/Account/` are always static SSR — do not add `@rendermode` to them.

## Don'ts
- Don't put interactive components in the server project — they work during prerender but fail after WebAssembly handoff.
- Don't inject `DbContext` or server-only services in `.Client` project components — use HTTP APIs instead.
- Don't assume execution environment — the same component runs on Server first, then WebAssembly later. Test both.
- Don't add `@rendermode InteractiveAuto` to pages — global interactivity is already configured in `App.razor`.
- Don't add `@rendermode` to Identity/Account pages if auth is configured — they must stay static SSR.
```

### 2. Remove default template pages
Delete `ShipmentTracker.Client/Pages/Counter.razor` and `ShipmentTracker.Client/Pages/Weather.razor`.

### 3. Create a Shipment model
Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Models/Shipment.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public class Shipment
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string TrackingNumber { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Origin { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Destination { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public ShipmentStatus Status { get; set; }
    public DateTime ShippedDate { get; set; }
    public DateTime EstimatedDelivery { get; set; }
    public string CustomerEmail { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Description { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}

public enum ShipmentStatus
{
    Pending,
    PickedUp,
    InTransit,
    OutForDelivery,
    Delivered,
    Delayed
}
```

### 4. Create the service interface
Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/IShipmentService.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public interface IShipmentService
{
    Task<List<Shipment>> GetAllShipmentsAsync();
    Task<Shipment?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber);
    Task<Shipment> CreateShipmentAsync(Shipment shipment);
    Task<Shipment> UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus status);
}
```

### 5. Create the client-side HTTP implementation
Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/ShipmentHttpService.cs`:
```csharp
using System.Net.Http.Json;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

public class ShipmentHttpService : IShipmentService
{
    private readonly HttpClient _http;

    public ShipmentHttpService(HttpClient http)
    {
        _http = http;
    }

    public async Task<List<Shipment>> GetAllShipmentsAsync()
    {
        return await _http.GetFromJsonAsync<List<Shipment>>("api/shipments") ?? new();
    }

    public async Task<Shipment?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber)
    {
        return await _http.GetFromJsonAsync<Shipment?>($"api/shipments/track/{trackingNumber}");
    }

    public async Task<Shipment> CreateShipmentAsync(Shipment shipment)
    {
        var response = await _http.PostAsJsonAsync("api/shipments", shipment);
        response.EnsureSuccessStatusCode();
        return await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<Shipment>() ?? shipment;
    }

    public async Task<Shipment> UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus status)
    {
        var response = await _http.PutAsJsonAsync($"api/shipments/{id}/status", status);
        response.EnsureSuccessStatusCode();
        return await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<Shipment>() ?? new();
    }
}
```

### 6. Register HttpClient and service in client Program.cs
Edit `ShipmentTracker.Client/Program.cs` to add:
```csharp
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.WebAssembly.Hosting;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

var builder = WebAssemblyHostBuilder.CreateDefault(args);

builder.Services.AddAuthorizationCore();
builder.Services.AddCascadingAuthenticationState();
builder.Services.AddAuthenticationStateDeserialization();

builder.Services.AddHttpClient("ShipmentTracker.ServerAPI", client =>
    client.BaseAddress = new Uri(builder.HostEnvironment.BaseAddress));
builder.Services.AddScoped(sp => sp.GetRequiredService<IHttpClientFactory>().CreateClient("ShipmentTracker.ServerAPI"));
builder.Services.AddScoped<IShipmentService, ShipmentHttpService>();

await builder.Build().RunAsync();
```

### 7. Create server-side service implementation
Create `ShipmentTracker/Services/ShipmentServerService.cs`:
```csharp
using Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;
using ShipmentTracker.Data;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Services;

public class ShipmentServerService : IShipmentService
{
    private readonly ApplicationDbContext _db;

    public ShipmentServerService(ApplicationDbContext db)
    {
        _db = db;
    }

    public async Task<List<Shipment>> GetAllShipmentsAsync()
    {
        return await _db.Shipments.OrderByDescending(s => s.ShippedDate).ToListAsync();
    }

    public async Task<Shipment?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber)
    {
        return await _db.Shipments.FirstOrDefaultAsync(s => s.TrackingNumber == trackingNumber);
    }

    public async Task<Shipment> CreateShipmentAsync(Shipment shipment)
    {
        _db.Shipments.Add(shipment);
        await _db.SaveChangesAsync();
        return shipment;
    }

    public async Task<Shipment> UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus status)
    {
        var shipment = await _db.Shipments.FindAsync(id) ?? throw new InvalidOperationException("Shipment not found");
        shipment.Status = status;
        await _db.SaveChangesAsync();
        return shipment;
    }
}
```

### 8. Add Shipments DbSet to ApplicationDbContext
The file is at `ShipmentTracker/Data/ApplicationDbContext.cs`. Add:
```csharp
public DbSet<Shipment> Shipments => Set<Shipment>();
```
And add `using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;` at the top.

### 9. Create API endpoints
Create `ShipmentTracker/Endpoints/ShipmentEndpoints.cs`:
```csharp
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Endpoints;

public static class ShipmentEndpoints
{
    public static void MapShipmentEndpoints(this WebApplication app)
    {
        var group = app.MapGroup("api/shipments");

        group.MapGet("/", async (IShipmentService service) =>
            Results.Ok(await service.GetAllShipmentsAsync()))
            .RequireAuthorization();

        group.MapGet("/track/{trackingNumber}", async (string trackingNumber, IShipmentService service) =>
        {
            var shipment = await service.GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(trackingNumber);
            return shipment is null ? Results.NotFound() : Results.Ok(shipment);
        }).RequireAuthorization();

        group.MapPost("/", async (Shipment shipment, IShipmentService service) =>
        {
            var created = await service.CreateShipmentAsync(shipment);
            return Results.Created($"api/shipments/{created.Id}", created);
        }).RequireAuthorization();

        group.MapPut("/{id}/status", async (int id, ShipmentStatus status, IShipmentService service) =>
        {
            var updated = await service.UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(id, status);
            return Results.Ok(updated);
        }).RequireAuthorization();
    }
}
```

### 10. Register server service and map endpoints in server Program.cs
Edit `ShipmentTracker/Program.cs`:
- Add `using ShipmentTracker.Services;` and `using ShipmentTracker.Endpoints;` and `using ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;`
- After `builder.Services.AddSingleton<IEmailSender<ApplicationUser>, IdentityNoOpEmailSender>();` add:
  ```csharp
  builder.Services.AddScoped<IShipmentService, ShipmentServerService>();
  ```
- Before `app.Run();` add:
  ```csharp
  app.MapShipmentEndpoints();
  ```

### 11. Create the Dispatcher Dashboard page
Replace `ShipmentTracker.Client/Pages/Home.razor` with a dispatcher dashboard that shows all shipments in a table with status badges, filtering by status, and a button to create new shipments. Include `@attribute [Authorize]`.

Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Pages/Home.razor`:
```razor
@page "/"
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization
@using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models
@using ShipmentTracker.Client.Services
@attribute [Authorize]
@inject IShipmentService ShipmentService

<PageTitle>Dispatcher Dashboard</PageTitle>

<h1>Shipment Dashboard</h1>

<div class="mb-3 d-flex gap-2 align-items-center">
    <label for="statusFilter" class="form-label mb-0">Filter by status:</label>
    <select id="statusFilter" class="form-select w-auto" @bind="selectedFilter">
        <option value="">All</option>
        @foreach (var status in Enum.GetValues<ShipmentStatus>())
        {
            <option value="@status">@status</option>
        }
    </select>
    <button class="btn btn-primary ms-auto" @onclick="ShowCreateForm">+ New Shipment</button>
</div>

@if (showCreateForm)
{
    <div class="card mb-3">
        <div class="card-body">
            <h5 class="card-title">Create New Shipment</h5>
            <div class="row g-2">
                <div class="col-md-3">
                    <input class="form-control" placeholder="Origin" @bind="newShipment.Origin" />
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-3">
                    <input class="form-control" placeholder="Destination" @bind="newShipment.Destination" />
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-3">
                    <input class="form-control" placeholder="Customer Email" @bind="newShipment.CustomerEmail" />
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-3">
                    <input class="form-control" placeholder="Description" @bind="newShipment.Description" />
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="mt-2">
                <button class="btn btn-success" @onclick="CreateShipment">Create</button>
                <button class="btn btn-secondary ms-2" @onclick="() => showCreateForm = false">Cancel</button>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
}

@if (shipments is null)
{
    <p><em>Loading shipments...</em></p>
}
else if (!FilteredShipments.Any())
{
    <p>No shipments found.</p>
